; An unbound relation head in a `:match` premise.
;
; `?R` is not a parameter, so the activator cannot bind it, and a rule
; compiles once per activator (Q29). Compiled anyway, the premise would give
; no steps — the plan's only premise gone, `steps` empty, and the matcher
; reads an empty step list as one VACUOUS match — so the rule would fire
; unconditionally and store its conclusion.
;
; The loader refuses a relation variable no parameter binds, at the top
; level as inside a pattern, before any rule is compiled (a rule shape
; that reads nothing, in silence). A relation is named by a name
; or by a parameter its activator binds.
;
(relation p Thing :why "p holds of {?1}")

(rule uses-free-head (?S)
  :match  (?R ?x)
  :assert (p ?x) :why "{?x} is in some relation ?R that no parameter binds, so p holds of {?x}")

(uses-free-head p)
